# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.cursor/mcp.json

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/

# Satellites colocated state (V5 .satellites/ pattern — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
# .satellites/ is purely operational: the CLI binary, satellites.toml,
# logs, and the worktree. It is NOT a source location — the committed
# substrate sources live under config/<workspace_id>/<project_id>/{documents,
# skills,principles}/ and are pushed via `satellites {document,skill,principle}
# upload`. Use `.satellites/*` (glob) not `.satellites/` (directory) so the
# seed carve-out below still takes effect.
.satellites/*
# Workspace/project seeds remain a committed source pushed via
# `satellites seed push`. Each *.md declares its identity; the substrate is
# the store, these files are the reviewable source (not a pull-mirror).
!.satellites/seeds/

# Operator-supplied config — may contain OAuth client secrets. The
# `*.example` templates stay in git; the live files do not.
/scripts/satellites-server.toml
/satellites.toml
